e><surname>Carver</surname><given-names>CS</given-names></name><name><surname>Pozo</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><name><surname>Noriega</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Scheier</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Robinson</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Ketcham</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name><name><surname>Moffat</surname><given-names>FL</given-names></name><name><surname>Clark</surname><given-names>KC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>How Coping Mediates the Effect of Optimism on Distress &#x02013; a Study of Women with Early-Stage Breast-Cancer</article-title><source>Journal of Personality and Social Psychology</source><year>1993</year><volume>65</volume><fpage>375</fpage><lpage>390</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8366426</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1037/0022-3514.65.2.375</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Folkman</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Moskowitz</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Positive affect and the other side of coping</article-title><source>American Psychologist</source><year>2000</year><volume>55</volume><fpage>647</fpage><lpage>654</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10892207</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1037/0003-066X.55.6.647</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thompson</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Gustafson</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Hamlett</surname><given-names>KW</given-names></name><name><surname>Spock</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stress, Coping, and Family Functioning in the Psyc